-- title:
--   Exists Ld Soundness
-- statement:
--   There exist universal real constants $a,b$ with $1\le a$, $0<b\le1$ such that for every low-degree parameter package $P$, error $\varepsilon>0$, and projective strategy $S$ whose game value is at least $1-\varepsilon$, there are polynomial POVMs $G_A,G_B$ satisfying all three point-polynomial, polynomial-point, and polynomial-polynomial consistency bounds. Each bound is at most
--
--   $$\delta_{\mathrm{LD}}(a,b,\varepsilon;P.q,P.m,P.d,P.k).$$
--
--   $P$ supplies the field and degree parameters, $S$ is the tested strategy, and $G_A,G_B$ are the extracted measurements. This is the compact low-degree soundness theorem.
